  "version": 8,
  "status": "published",
  "description_nl": "2026-10-06: ITR-1 (Sahaj): a resident with total income up to 50 lakh from salary or pension, up to two houses, other sources, 112A gains up to 1.25 lakh and farm income up to 5,000; anything else - not resident, more income, other gains or losses, a directorship, unlisted shares, foreign assets, losses carried - is ITR-2. The first reason that applies is the one shown. 2026-10-06: presumptive business or profession income (44AD / 44ADA) with nothing ITR-1 would refuse is ITR-4 (Sugam); with more (other gains, a third house, foreign assets ...) or receipts over the limit it is ITR-3. 2026-10-06: huf - ITR-1 is for individuals; an HUF without business files ITR-2 (with presumptive business, ITR-4). 2026-10-07: winnings from lottery / races / gambling / online games, or a virtual digital asset transferred: ITR-1 and ITR-4 cannot hold them - ITR-2 (ITR-3 with business income). 2026-10-07: test cases for AY 2026-27 ITR-1 / ITR-4: 112A gains up to 1.25 lakh only with no capital loss brought or carried forward; any other capital gain - ITR-2 (ITR-3 with a business). 2026-10-07: books - business or profession income from the person's own profit and loss (no presumptive basis): ITR-3 (why_biz_books). 2026-10-07: clubbing (s.64): income of a spouse / minor child clubbed - ITR-2 (ITR-3 with a business), for Schedule SPI; ITR-1 / ITR-4 are open to clubbed income but have no schedule naming whose it is - My return files ITR-2, which any individual may file instead. resident means resident AND ordinarily resident: an RNOR or a non-resident files ITR-2 / ITR-3 (ITR-1 / ITR-4 are for an ordinarily resident).",
